# Still starting: bit 2 of every byte of RAM (IC3's column IO4) is stuck low, so the ROM's start-up, which clears the RAM and checks it back, never ends: the pattern the TV shows while it does so stays for ever. The keyboard is never read.
machine bw80
title "Still starting"
brief "At power-on the TV shows the usual moment of moving pattern, but it never goes away: no picture, no cursor, and the keys do nothing."
fault column IC3.IO4 0
